  "body": "## Status: reproduced; actual-merge certification pending\nThis prospective campaign proves unit barriers for admitted binary roots with exactly two star children, arbitrary child degrees >=2 and k>=2. It does not establish a universal unit-barrier theorem; chains and higher-degree roots remain unresolved.\n\nThe construction normalizes the two branches sequentially to a common profile-specific canonical endpoint while keeping total excursion at most one. The three primary barriers remain independent scalar minima; LEX is diagnostic.\n\n- Verified integrated parent: f685af0d8465b35d52c600ab5a8c8b8a1cbcd070.\n- Immutable prospective preregistration: 377094a964a351d408af4ed869d708711c181fc0.\n- Scientific source: 85b199712c2a2dcd13059fba6b9ebbdcc64d71af.\n- Publication head: 4657489a7fab2b2adcf341f78167ef9e99a95069.\n- [Source and independent fresh reproduction](https://github.com/proteinfoldingengine/WetLabEngine/actions/runs/36808557315): successful.\n- 600 passing checks (531 inherited +69 new), full inherited replay and fresh parent canonical reconstruction.\n- Six complete graphs: 223,584 states, 1,585,329 edges, 43 profiles, 139 representative normalizations, 787 component pairs including 682 sibling-active pairs. Zero construction failures and zero nonunit pairs.\n- Both API-bound artifacts retained losslessly; all 174 publication members verified against SHA256 manifests and Git blobs. All 21 scientific files agree byte-for-byte.\n\nIndependent fresh executions ran concurrently on separate runners; this removes serial waiting without reusing scientific outputs. Content-addressed source snapshots preserve all 1,499 source/input paths using 1,322 unique objects. Prospective EXECUTION_PLAN.md records both optimizations.\n\nMathematical/source and artifact review passed. Exact-head merge, actual-merge full replay, and durable audited receipt remain required before CLOSED/CERTIFIED.",
